# Intent: Face turning. The seeker's setting turn_to_faces has three modes: off (never), talk (only after the wake word and during a talk) and always (also an idle watch: one camera frame a second, a turn when something moves, at most four turns a minute, the camera cue with every frame). The default was talk, so the unit never looked up when someone walked in. The default is now always, and the seeker is safe to leave on: it runs nothing while the unit is locked or carried (every mode) and its idle watch waits for day (night mode), besides the gates it already had (asleep, muted, full quiet, vision off, a host's look lease). A wake word at night still turns the head, slowly. A person who chose talk or off keeps that choice.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_seek_core.h, maipai_seek_wire_core.h, maipai_seek.cc, maipai_prefs_core.h, maipai_tbprefs.cc, maipai_tbprefs.h (ours)
# Check after a flash: self.prefs.get shows turn_to_faces always on a unit that never chose; walking into view turns the head once with the camera cue; locked, carried and night mode stop it (self.look.status shows no new watch frames).
# Kconfig: none

diff --git a/firmware/main/hal/maipai_seek_core.h b/firmware/main/hal/maipai_seek_core.h
